.SH "Member Data Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "boolean hasDgram"

.PP
True when an established connection supports native UDP or WebTransport datagrams\&. 
.SS "string localAddr"

.PP
the ip address of the local end of the connection 
.SS "number localPort"

.PP
the port that the local end of the connection is communicating over 
.SS "string remoteAddr"

.PP
the ip address of the remote end of the connection 
.SS "number remotePort"

.PP
the port that the remote end of the connection is communicating over 
.SS "boolean secure"

.PP
Read-only indication that the carrier uses TLS\&. True for wss://, false for ws:// and native TCP\&. Browser localAddr and remoteAddr are empty strings; localPort and remotePort are zero because browser APIs do not expose socket endpoints\&. Native runtimes populate the available endpoints\&. 
.SS "string transport"

.PP
Read-only carrier name: native or websocket\&. \fBonMessage()\fP continues to report "tcp" for reliable messages and "udp" for native datagrams\&. Inspect transport to identify the carrier\&. WebSocket reports hasDgram as false, so \fBsendDgram()\fP uses \fBsend()\fP\&. 

